// here describes a card, a row or a cell. Surfaces embed FailureKind in their
// own resolved props and render it their own way — the feed's card
// (failure-card.proto), the footer's row (footer.proto), the roster's notice
// (sidebar.proto). One vocabulary, per-surface carriers, exactly as
// tokens.proto is one economics vocabulary behind several resolved views.
//
// WHY KINDS AND NOT A CLASS PLUS A STRING. A failure is a CONDITION, and a
// condition is what a oneof is for. Naming the kind on the wire means a
// consumer that meets an unfamiliar failure fails to match it instead of
// silently rendering it as something else, and it means each kind carries the
// evidence that kind actually has rather than a shared free-text field that
// every producer packs differently and every consumer parses differently.
//
